  "body": {
    "id": "prop:equality-frontier",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For either \\(b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}\\in\\{b^{\\mathrm{OVS}},b^{\\mathrm{const}}\\}\\),\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Var}_P\\{b^{\\mathrm{cmp}\\prime}\\Psi_P(O)\\}-V_{\\mathrm{agg}}\n=E_P[(b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}-b^\\star(X))'\\Gamma_P(X)(b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}-b^\\star(X))],\n\\]\nwhereas its loss relative to the full semiparametric bound is\n\\[\n\\Delta(b^{\\mathrm{cmp}})\n=E_P[(b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}-b^\\star(X))'\\Gamma_P(X)(b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}-b^\\star(X))]\n+\\Delta_{\\mathrm{normal}}(P).\n\\]\nEquality with the aggregate score-family optimum holds if and only if\n\\[\nN'\\Gamma_P(X)b^{\\mathrm{cmp}}=0\n\\qquad P_X\\text{-almost surely}.\n\\]\nEquality with the full semiparametric bound holds if and only if\n\\[\nE_P[Z_P^{\\mathrm{per}}(O)\\{b^{\\mathrm{cmp}\\prime}\\Psi_P(O)\\}\\mid X]=0\n\\qquad P_X\\text{-almost surely}.\n\\]\nThus the aggregate KKT residual and the complete-normal residual answer two different equality questions.",
    "free_symbols": [
